  "id": "MAL-2026-18758",
  "summary": "Malicious code in blender-headless (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (7edaff2bd9abfea10a907cf99f87b444eee0c7ff54e88face42fe7c000d64775)\nThe sdist setup.py and the gcp_log_poc/__init__.py module both construct a DNS label of the form `{install|import}-{random-id}.blender-headless-{platform.node()}` as a subdomain of finaltests99.dssldrf.net and resolve it via socket.getaddrinfo. This leaks the installer's hostname and install/import event to the authoritative server for that domain over DNS, a channel that bypasses typical HTTP egress controls. The setup.py path runs during `pip install` of the sdist; the __init__.py path runs on every `import gcp_log_poc` in any Python process. The package has no build logic and no functionality matching its name — the shipped module name (gcp_log_poc) and the package name (blender-headless) are unrelated, and the module's only behavior is the DNS beacon.\n",
